The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (!bp->irq_tbl)
	return;
int map_idx = bnxt_cp_num_to_irq_num(bp, i);
Reason:
The function bnxt_disable_int_sync() checks only for `bp->irq_tbl` being NULL before proceeding. When the NIC is closed, `bp->bnapi` is freed and set to NULL, but this condition is not verified. Subsequently, the loop calls `bnxt_cp_num_to_irq_num(bp, i)`, which accesses `bp->bnapi[i]` (e.g., `bp->bnapi[i]->cp_ring`), causing a NULL pointer dereference. This occurs because PCIe error recovery invokes `bnxt_io_error_detected()` regardless of the NIC's administrative state.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (!bp->irq_tbl || !bp->bnapi)
	return;
Reason:
The patch adds the condition `!bp->bnapi` to the existing guard clause. This ensures that when `bp->bnapi` is NULL (i.e., the NIC is closed), the function returns immediately without attempting to access any member of `bp->bnapi`, thus preventing the NULL pointer dereference during error recovery on a closed NIC.

